CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*lvalue-reference specialization selected.*FAILURE.*$
^.*rvalue-reference specialization selected.*FAILURE.*$
--
Class-template partial specialization keyed on the argument's reference
qualifier (`S<T&>` vs `S<T&&>`), N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match] /
[temp.deduct.type].  Template-argument deduction must distinguish an
lvalue-reference pattern from an rvalue-reference pattern; previously CBMC
matched either pattern against any reference argument, selecting the wrong
specialization (and, for libstdc++'s `__common_ref_impl<_Xp&, _Yp&&>` family,
producing a self-inheriting base).  See
doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.
